  "text": "Pip helped prepare the dough and similar-sized loaves. Rina baked the bread she had promised.\n\nYou saw the repair, the baking and Rina’s thanks. Talk to Sol about the story he has started.\n\nSol says: “Later, she came to my workshop with a loaf of bread. She brought it to thank me.”\n\nMara says: “I’d like to listen while you read it. I’ll join you after the passengers leave.”\n\nFirst the bread, then her visit. Now I can follow what happened after you left the bakery.\n\nThis end doesn't reach the bank yet. Move the sections so the crossing reaches both sides.\n\nI could hear that rain as you read. I’m glad to hear what happened to the flour afterward.\n\nMara will still be working at the usual time. Start later or choose Pip to read her story.\n\nThe copy is in Pip’s backpack. Walk back across the footbridge to Mara and give it to her.\n\nThe tape is beside the tear. The wing is still loose. Move the same strip across the tear.\n\nRina takes one baked loaf to thank Sol. The other bread stays for the people she promised.\n\nWater has stopped entering the bakery. Rain still falls outside. Let Rina check her flour.\n\nSol says: “I’ll bring your suggested ending. We can show the part of my story you chose.”\n\nSol says: “I'll bring this version to the garden. I'd like people to hear what happened.”\n\nThe cushions are on the bench. Grandma can now finish the story of why she put them away.\n\nWe haven't asked Sol whether he'd like to share a story. Find him at Rina’s bakery first.\n\nRina came to my workshop with a loaf of bread. She brought it to thank me for the repair.\n\nA separate part of something larger. Here, each wooden section is part of the footbridge.\n\nThe seed is safe at the landing. Grandma is coming to collect it; Pip can keep exploring.",
